   "id": "13_operate",
   "text": "Lesson nine's question: who operates it? An agent works that nightly reconcile. It gets its own identity, and the least access the job needs: it reads the ledger, and the processor's report. It can't move money, or change the ledger. Every action is logged. [pause] One night, an upgrade shows two charges: two browser tabs, two quotes, two keys. The agent flags it. A person refunds it. And the miss becomes a fourth check: one open quote per subscription.",
